<description>&lt;p&gt;Colombia opened an embassy in Jerusalem while UN independent experts urged Ecopetrol to provide reparations to armed-conflict victims, and the UN Security Council heard calls for the peace deal to endure as insecurity grows. Opposition groups launched protests against de la Espriella’s budget cuts, and the peace tribunal charged former FARC members with anti-Indigenous crimes. Budget cuts threaten the peace court and searches for the disappeared, officials say. Rebels detonated a car bomb outside a toll booth in Cauca, and FARC dissidents were killed in a Catatumbo operation and an army airstrike that also hit a teenager. 225 battle-related deaths were recorded in 2024, according to UCDP.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Machine-written from the linked sources, checked for figures and names not in them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://news.un.org/feed/view/en/story/2026/10/1168580&quot;&gt;UN News&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;Al Jazeera&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiV0FVX3lxTE9iQ3JyeU1lQjBqOUtqcHZvOHRENnJpRnJzODNtZk1qSm02U002OXp2Vm5odkVpRTZpNWRXNTFOZENaeUtNU3NzLVhsNGdNZnBUcmdJdTFXSQ?oc=5&quot;&gt;UN News&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;Al Jazeera&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiuAFBVV95cUxObUVqdXVtVUFCMDgyZ3c2dVptc2dndnQzTjdIRE9VLUM3MXMySDlfY2FqQkFfbmZyVGI2WkZIc0VyN2VmSTF1TEVqYXdNTEY4TDU2MHRlajlxem1mX29ta1p4NW1jUnBsZUQ4UjkyN1hPaWpzekpiYzV1bldQTi0tT1h3MVdLd28tR1FSY0pXVE9mTnV1WGlxNzlVM0lDLVdhYW5uQjhpckE1aVBoZ0hNb3hJLUlMdjZs0gG-AUFVX3lxTFBzYVVYZnBpQnFlMEFUQ3RCb2NrMERyQkhGQ1VCM0lIWm5zaXM5QkV6S2ZlQnpmNHZmNHROSXE1eHZYQ21waVFCVHJpZVd0c3BaQ3ZQUFduRkdlS1psczc5MXp5TWZOcDZmN2cwZlNDM185Y0hQbWtYcDlURk14TnhSeExrVm1NVndyRFJpcTRKVUNpOUsyTG9FejhMeEJ6WnpVRm05M0lKT3c1OEV5Nk84dUdGcDFmLXZTQnFZMmc?oc=5&quot;&gt;Al Jazeera&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiyAFBVV95cUxQQlJ3ZUw3Z